WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.501
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.970
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.138
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.406
Well, after marrying
his cousin,

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.675
giving a press conference
at a landscaping company,

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.146
and almost masturbating
in the "Borat" movie,

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:17.517
Rudy Giuliani
has finally slipped up.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.119
That's right.
A jury in Washington, D.C.,

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.956
last week ordered Rudy Giuliani
to pay nearly $150 million

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.258
in the defamation case
brought against him

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.926
by two Georgia election workers.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:31.798
Okay, but he<i> for sure</i>
doesn't have that much money.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:36.402
You might as well order a dog
to drive you to the airport.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:37.804
A lot of stress for the dog,

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.874
but you're not getting
to the airport.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.274
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:44.143
was formally nominated
over the weekend

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.446
to run in the 2024 presidential
election.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.947
Said Putin,
"If anyone has any questions,

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:51.284
my window is always open.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:01:00.260
He's prone to defenestration.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.462
In a new interview, presidential
hopeful Robert F. Kennedy Jr.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.498
says that he thinks people
should be able

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.433
to debate the legitimacy
of the election

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.935
without being dismissed
as crazy.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.871
Oh, buddy, that's not why
people think you're crazy.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.205
You can debate the election.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.476
What you can't do
is work out in blue jeans.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.682
A Senate staffer was fired
over the weekend

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:27.019
for allegedly filming a sex tape
inside a committee hearing room.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.255
It's the first time
anyone in that room

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.224
has ever come together.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.600
Former UN ambassador Nikki Haley

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.769
criticized former president
Trump in a new interview

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.370
and said that he had
the opportunity

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.906
to stop the Capitol attack,
and before that,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:51.277
he had an opportunity not to
start it.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.979
According to the latest data
released from Pornhub,

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:59.785
the search term "granny"
increased in popularity by 132%

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.353
because what better
to hear after

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:04.724
"Who's your Daddy?"
than "I can't remember."

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.498
Same dude wrote that
as that "come together" joke.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.303
We should check
his search history.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.505
Or not.
Yeah. Or not.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.108
Officials in New Mexico
have begun testing wastewater

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.676
at some high schools
for illicit drugs,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.346
and found that most schools
tested positive for cocaine.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.846
And it has to be
the students,

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:32.284
because there's no way
a teacher can afford cocaine.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:34.720
Today it was Rolling Stones
guitarist Keith Richards'

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.155
80th birthday.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:39.592
Even crazier, he celebrated by
going to lunch with his parents.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.465
And finally, two seemingly
drunk men in Australia

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.468
were arrested after they climbed
into a construction site,

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:52.605
threw bags of concrete off
the scaffolding, fell asleep,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.507
and then refused
to get down for eight hours.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.642
Officials first suspected
they were drunk

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.145
when they were Australian.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.445
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:04.317
We're up and running.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.187
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.854
You know him from
one of the best shows

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.422
of the last few years,
"The Bear."

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:12.458
Currently, he stars
in "The Iron Claw,"

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.626
which is in theaters
this weekend.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:17.130
Jeremy Allen White
is back on the show.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.031
So excited.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.333
And you know her best
from her Emmy-winning role

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.002
"on Ted Lasso."

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.637
Her special,
"Home for Christmas,"

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.205
is on Apple TV+ now.

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.574
The great Hannah Waddingham
will also be joining us.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:33.146
So excited, you guys.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:38.684
I went to
the Big Apple Circus yesterday

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:40.886
in New York City.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:44.157
It was amazing.
I'm just being serious here.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.226
I was not looking forward to it.
I had the best time.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.696
My only regret,
should have brought my kids.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.767
I did bring my kids.
It's the best time

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.135
I've had with my kids
in like a year.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.838
It was unbelievable.
It's a circus theater, Roncalli.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:02.275
It's a German outfit.
They're a German circus.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.610
Don't worry about
the language barrier.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.680
I don't know if you've been to
a circus -- almost no talking.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.914
The clowns try to tell you
things,

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:10.617
but it's a lot of like...

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.222
I can't -- I know
I'm talking about it.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:20.159
You might be thinking, "Seth,
we all know circuses are great."

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:23.696
This circus is so [bleep] great.
Juggling.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.932
I don't know why
I've been sleeping on juggling.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.367
When I was seven,
I loved juggling,

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.469
and then I started thinking --
I started being snarky

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:31.837
and thinking there were
better things.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.472
Well, let me tell you,
I've spent the last 40 years

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:34.874
looking for something better.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.810
Nothing's better.
And I'll tell you this.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.680
These were a bunch
of German circus people.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.648
Do I think they could do my job?

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:46.119
I know this -- they could do it
better than I could do theirs.

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:54.226
It was so good.

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:57.129
You got to go to the circus,
you guys.

00:04:57.129 --> 00:05:02.000
No animals,
which is great.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.803
Not just for the animals,

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:06.572
who I don't think
ever had a lot of fun.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.808
It's no circus for them.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:15.014
Here's the thing, though.
I'm happy for the animals.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.284
It's doesn't smell terrible.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.452
It used to be you walked
into a circus tent

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:23.856
and you were just met
with a wall of animals.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.726
It was great. Gotta go
to the circus, you guys.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.260
I know I'm talking too much
about the circus,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.763
but it's so good.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.197
And by the way, no animals.

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:33.832
Except then three dudes
come out,

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:35.267
beginning in the second
half of the circus --

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.436
By the way, two halves.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.703
My kids don't like
two halves of anything.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.172
During the intermission,
I said to my kids,

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.539
"We could go home now."
One of my --

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.941
My seven-year-old
looked at me in the eye

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:46.312
and said,
"I don't ever want this to end."

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.513
The five year old said,

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:52.952
"I want to join the circus,"
and we let him.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:56.189
I don't know when I'm going
to see him again,

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:58.524
but if I -- when I do, he's
going to be tightrope walking

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.227
and it will have been worth it.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.995
But these three --
second act starts

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.531
and it's three guys
in a polar bear suits,

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.966
big polar bear suits,
and they walk out.

00:06:07.966 --> 00:06:10.002
And it was great
because I knew right away

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:13.205
they weren't real polar bears,
but the suits were good enough

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.474
that my kids looked at me
and were like, are those real?

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.843
And then I got to look at them
and I was like, no.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.912
And then that's great
because they're like, oh, cool.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.716
Dad knows stuff about bears.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.284
And that for me
is really rewarding

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.919
because usually I don't know
[bleep].

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:31.891
Guys, go to the circus.

